<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Digit handles information in connection with digit.software."
  path="/privacy"
  updated="September 20, 2026"
>
      <section>
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>This Privacy Policy describes how Digit ("Digit," "we," "us," or "our") handles information in
          connection with this website, <a href="https://digit.software/">digit.software</a> (the "Website").
          This policy applies only to the Website and does not extend to any other Digit product, service, or
          business practice not described here.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Information We May Receive</h2>
        <p>The Website is a static informational site. We do not operate user accounts, checkout systems, or
          customer databases through the Website, and we do not knowingly collect sensitive personal
          information through it.</p>
        <p>If you contact us directly (for example, by emailing <a href="mailto:info@digit.software">info@digit.software</a>), we receive whatever information you
          choose to include in that message, such as your email address and the contents of your
          communication. We use that information only to respond to you.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Website and Technical Data</h2>
        <p>Like most websites, ordinary technical information may be processed automatically as part of
          serving web pages (for example, IP address, browser type, device type, referring page, and the
          pages requested). This Website is hosted on GitHub Pages, a third-party hosting service; GitHub
          processes standard web request data as necessary to deliver the Website, subject to GitHub's own
          privacy practices.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
        <p>The Website does not set its own cookies and does not use tracking pixels, analytics scripts, or
          advertising technologies. The underlying hosting infrastructure may use technical mechanisms
          necessary to serve the site reliably; we do not control those independently of GitHub Pages' own
          infrastructure.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How Information Is Used</h2>
        <p>Any information we receive directly from you (such as through an email you send us) is used solely
          to respond to your inquiry and for legitimate related business purposes, such as recordkeeping.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>The Website is hosted on GitHub Pages. We do not integrate third-party analytics, advertising, or
          embedded widgets on the Website. If that changes in the future, this policy will be updated
          accordingly.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Data Sharing</h2>
        <p>We do not sell personal information. We do not share information you send us with third parties
          except where necessary to operate the Website (such as our hosting provider processing standard
          technical request data) or where required by law.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Data Retention</h2>
        <p>We retain direct correspondence (such as emails sent to info@digit.software) for as long as
          reasonably necessary to address the inquiry and for legitimate recordkeeping purposes.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Data Security</h2>
        <p>We take reasonable measures to protect information we handle, but no method of transmission or
          storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>External Links</h2>
        <p>The Website may reference or link to third-party resources. We are not responsible for the privacy
          practices or content of any third-party site.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>The Website is not directed to children, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from
          children.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date above reflects the
          most recent revision.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about this Privacy Policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:info@digit.software">info@digit.software</a>.</p>
      </section>
    
</LegalLayout>
